      "quality_notes": "Resend transactional-email API. Free tier: 3000 emails/month, 100/day. Wrapper defaults sender to onboarding@resend.dev (Resend's owned shared sender) and refuses real-domain senders without explicit RESEND_ALLOW_REAL_DOMAINS=true opt-in. Test addresses (delivered@/bounced@/complained@resend.dev) produce deterministic webhook events without sending real email. Wrapper-level success state is status='queued'; delivery / bounce / complaint state arrives via webhook later (out of scope for v1).",
      "gotchas": [
        "Real-domain senders require RESEND_ALLOW_REAL_DOMAINS=true; @resend.dev defaults work without the opt-in.",
        "Sets Idempotency-Key header from ProviderRequest.idempotency_key \u2014 identical requests within 24 hours return the same email id.",
        "Recipient accepted as either string or list of strings; wrapper normalises to list for the API call.",
        "Test mode (test_mode=true) is detected when both from AND all recipients live on @resend.dev.",
        "Cost projection uses paid-tier rate ($0.0004/email) even on the free tier so cap math is conservative."
